{"query":"What instruments are on Southern Hydrate Ridge?","answer":"The Southern Hydrate Ridge node of the OOI Regional Cabled Array carries a diverse, cabled instrument suite that monitors seismic activity, acoustic signals, water‑column and seafloor currents, visual and chemical conditions, and fluid flow.\n\nSeismology  \n- Broadband Ocean Bottom Seismometer (Guralp CMG‑1T5T) – records regional earthquakes.  \n- Short‑period Seismometers (Guralp CMG‑1 sec) – three units; record regional earthquakes, local cracking events, and support studies of methane‑pumping dynamics.  \n- Summit Seismic Stations HYS11, HYS12, HYS13, HYS14 – dedicated seismometers at the summit, used for regional earthquake monitoring and local seismicity.  \n- Broadband OBS (referenced but instrument document unresolved) – mentioned in the inventory but details are not available in the retrieved evidence.\n\nAcoustics  \n- Low‑Frequency Hydrophone (HTI 90‑U) – mounted on the flank; measures T‑waves, general ocean acoustics, and marine mammal vocalizations.\n\nHydrography & Currents  \n- 3‑D Velocity Meter (Nobska MAVS‑4) – flank deployment; measures three‑dimensional local currents.  \n- ADCP 75 kHz (Teledyne RDI Workhorse LongRanger) – summit deployment; provides current profiles and tracks bubble‑plume dynamics.  \n- Summit ADCP (Teledyne RDI Workhorse LongRanger Monitor 75 kHz) – same sensor type as above, listed separately in the catalog.  \n- Seafloor Pressure sensor (Sea‑Bird SBE 54) – records tides, tsunami signatures, storms, and seafloor uplift/deflation.\n\nImaging & Visual Observation  \n- Digital Still Camera (SubC custom assembly, model CAMDSB103) – summit; captures bubble plume morphology, macro‑fauna, and microbial distribution.  \n\nFluid & Chemical Sampling  \n- Benthic Flow Meter (non‑commercial) – two units; quantifies fluid flow into and out of the seafloor for flux calculations.  \n- Osmotic Fluid Sampler (non‑commercial, TLR Inc. OsmoSampler) – measures fluid chemistry and contributes to flux estimates.  \n- Mass Spectrometer (non‑commercial, Harvard‑Girguis cabled Mass Spec) – summit; performs gas analyses for flux calculations.  \n- Summit Mass Spectrometer (cabled Mass Spec) – same instrument class as above, listed separately in the catalog.  \n- Benthic CDOM Fluorometer (Tryon UCSD CAT meter) – summit; measures colored dissolved organic matter.  \n- Benthic Fluorometer (Multi‑parameter, Solomon UW Mosquito benthic flow sampler) – summit; provides multi‑parameter fluorescence measurements.\n\nOther Sensors  \n- 3‑D Current Meter (Nobska MAVS‑4) – flank; listed again as “Flank 3D Current Meter” in the inventory.  \n\nThe evidence lists these instruments and their primary measurement capabilities. The retrieved records do not cover every possible sensor that may be present (e.g., additional temperature or salinity probes), so the inventory may be incomplete.","answer_model":"Groq GPT-OSS 120B","answer_citations":[{"id":"PAGE-ccbe15abdccfcd49","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge","url":"https://interactiveoceans.washington.edu/research-sites/southern-hydrate-ridge/"},{"id":"PAGE-0f61ae45e3fc0e6b","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge VISIONS ’14","url":"https://interactiveoceans.washington.edu/southern-hydrate-ridge-visions-14/"},{"id":"INSTRUMENT-405172352ab7462f08","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge Flank Low-Frequency Hydrophone","url":"https://oceanobservatories.org/site/rs01sum1/"},{"id":"INSTRUMENT-bd5b5f5c5b078717cc","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge Benthic CDOM Fluorometer","url":"https://dataexplorer.oceanobservatories.org/#ooi/array/RSMARGIN/instrument_type/FLUOR/data"},{"id":"INSTRUMENT-9b29bef70be5983985","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge Summit Seismic Station HYS12","url":"https://ds.iris.edu/mda/OO/HYS12/?starttime=2014-09-01T15:17:00&endtime=2599-12-31T23:59:59"},{"id":"INSTRUMENT-755d7fed67e3f89d49","title":"Southern Hydrate Ridge Summit ADCP","url":"https://oceanobservatories.org/site/rs01sum2/"},{"id":"INSTRUMENT-3b15c7f27c7b5c1